UNIT escape_markers
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@f68cca701417 cli/sir/canon.mjs escapeMarkers — the code is the truth
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG escape_markers(value: json) -> json
ENVELOPE any json value: none, bool, f64, text, list[json], map[text, json], nested to any depth (deeper than the cap
  throws, R1). The js file widens this to every host value of its runtime (array holes, non-map objects, wide integers, an absent value).
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Make a value an artifact RETURNED safe to grade: every map, at any depth, that holds one of the three codec
  marker keys "__t", "__throw", "__threw" is wrapped in the escape map {"__t": "obj", "v": <the map>}, so no returned
  value can ever read as a codec tag or as a throw. Everything else is rebuilt unchanged. The input is never modified.
  The js file widens the walk to the host's keyed collection and its set (both descended, never wrapped) and to values
  passed through.
BEHAVIOR
R1 DEPTH. The value itself is at depth 0; every element of a list and every value of a map is one deeper than its
  container (lists and maps count alike; an escape map added by R4 adds no depth). If any node that is visited lies
  at depth greater than 100 -> throws "a value nests deeper than 100". A scalar or an empty list or map counts as a
  visited node at its own depth: 100 lists around a scalar returns, 101 lists around a scalar throws; 100 lists
  around an empty list returns, 100 lists around a one-element list throws.
PINNED number MAX_VALUE_DEPTH = 100 CITED canon.mjs MAX_VALUE_DEPTH, the codec's one value-depth model (round 5, #78)
R2 SCALARS (none, bool, f64, text) -> returned unchanged.
R3 LIST -> a new list of the same length; each element is the result of this contract applied to it, at its depth.
R4 MAP -> a new map with the same keys in the same order, each value the result of this contract applied to it, at its
  depth. Then, if the INPUT map holds the key "__t", "__throw" or "__threw" -> the result is the two-entry map
  {"__t": "obj", "v": <that new map>} (keys in that order); otherwise the result is the new map itself.
R5 The escape is on the KEY's presence alone: the marker key's value may be any json (text, number, none, bool, list,
  map, empty text) and the map is still escaped; any other keys in the map do not matter. CITED FIDELITY package —
  wider than the codec's own marker rule (an own TEXT-valued key), which reads only text-valued markers as tags.
R6 Only the three exact keys trigger R4: look-alikes ("__T", "_t", "__t " with a trailing space, "__throws", "t",
  "threw", "v") never do. A map already shaped like an escape ({"__t": "obj", "v": ...}) is escaped again, as is
  the "v" map inside it if it holds a marker key.
INVARIANT the result never contains a map with a marker key other than an escape map {"__t": "obj", "v": m} whose own
  "__t" is the text "obj".
INVARIANT the input value is not modified; the result shares no list or map with it.
NOTE rust omitted: this unit's domain is the JS value model itself — which objects count as maps (plain vs class
  instances, prototype-less objects), own vs inherited and enumerable keys, array holes, the host's keyed collection
  and set (descended, never wrapped), values that pass through untouched (byte arrays, wide integers, the absent value). Over the abstract json envelope the contract is a small tree
  rebuild that rust could carry, but every driver that calls it is a js/ts driver (rust drivers escape with their own
  {ok}/{throw} envelope), so the JS envelope IS the contract. Tier 2 is js/ts only.
ORACLE value -> oracles/escape_markers.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 5224025b24b2f999a63aa557b1dfb09f97d5336319c4e050832527676934aade
SCOPE IN: R1–R6 over json values, plus the js file's widening (holes, Map and Set descent, pass-through of other non-plain values,
  own-key rule).
  OUT (graded): js-host values whose RESULT the js extension codec cannot encode — see the js file's GRADED line.
  OUT: the depth argument (the real export takes an internal second parameter, depth, that the seam never passes —
  it starts at 0), the codec's encode/decode of the escaped result, every rust driver.
PROVENANCE rederive@f68cca701417 (authority tree a1c4b88edc06; Set descent #153), cli/sir/canon.mjs export escapeMarkers (round 4
  selfhost #55 #58; round 5 #81 Map descent, #78 MAX_VALUE_DEPTH = 100); seam selfhost/seams/escape_markers.mjs.
